\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Jesus, the gift divine I know,
\par The gift divine I ask of Thee;
\par That living water now bestow,
\par Thy Spirit and Thyself, on me;
\par Thou, Lord, of life the Fountain art,
\par Now let me find Thee in my heart.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Thee let me drink, and thirst no more
\par For drops of finite happiness;
\par Spring up, O well, in heavenly power,
\par In streams of pure perennial peace,
\par In joy that none can take away,
\par In life which can for ever stay.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Father, on me the grace bestow,
\par Unblamable before Thy sight,
\par Whence all the streams of mercy flow;
\par Mercy, Thy own supreme delight,
\par To me for Jesu's sake, impart,
\par And plant Thy nature in my heart.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Thy mind throughout my life be shown,
\par While, listening to the sufferer's cry,
\par The window's and the orphan's groan,
\par On mercy's wings I swiftly fly,
\par The poor and helpless to relieve,
\par My life, my all, for them to give.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Thus may I show the Spirit within,
\par Which purges me from every stain;
\par Unspotted from the world and sin,
\par My faith is integrity maintain;
\par The truth of my religion prove 
\par By perfect purity and love.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

